WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.310
- House MD actually does clinic hours.

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.560
Let's see some of his wildest encounters.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:05.760
Huge thank you to Headspace

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.766
for sponsoring a part of today's video.

00:00:07.766 --> 00:00:08.599
(Mikhail exclaims)

00:00:08.599 --> 00:00:09.960
- My asthma.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.370
They said they'd fixed it,

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:13.410
but it didn't make any difference at all.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:14.640
- Asthma step up plan.

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.770
If you're using your
rescue inhaler too often,

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:18.120
AKA your Albuterol,

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:19.830
you might need a controller medication

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.510
to prevent the asthma
attacks from happening.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.760
Some people have specific
triggers that they can avoid

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.430
or they can take medicines
targeting those triggers.

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:28.740
You like to think about
allergy medicines for that.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:30.480
You could take your
traditional antihistamines

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.130
or maybe even a medication like Singulair.

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.020
You gotta think outside
the box with asthma.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:35.100
- Are you using your inhaler?

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.233
- All the time, go through one a week.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.420
- You sure you're using it right?

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:41.250
- A lot of patients, especially children,

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.660
tend to not use it correctly,

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.250
'cause they weren't properly educated.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.810
They would benefit from a spacer.

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:47.460
This is what a spacer looks like.

00:00:48.606 --> 00:00:49.951
(inhaler puffs)

00:00:49.951 --> 00:00:51.780
(Mikhail laughs)

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:53.430
Come on, there's images on the bottle

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:54.600
of what you're supposed to do.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.040
That's never gonna happen.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:59.280
- Experiencing fatigue and weakness.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.290
- Usually he's stronger than an ox.

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:02.827
- 102-year-old ox.

00:01:02.827 --> 00:01:03.750
(Mikhail laughs)

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:06.104
- 102-year-old ox, an elderly ox.

00:01:06.104 --> 00:01:06.937
(ox moos)

00:01:06.937 --> 00:01:09.270
- There's tingling in
his feet and his legs.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.490
I want a full battery of tests.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.680
- Well maybe we wanna
check if he's diabetic

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:15.480
because, in that case,
you could treat that

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.550
and you could change quality
of life tremendously.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:18.900
- Nice of you to float your friend.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:21.210
- He's not my friend, he's my father.

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:23.640
He's 22 years older than me.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:24.473
- Well that's true.

00:01:24.473 --> 00:01:26.910
He's definitely had his jowls done.

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:28.980
Statistically, if he
didn't have these symptoms,

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:30.900
he'd be like most people of his age,

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:32.700
dead for the past several decades.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.260
- Do the tests, I'm sick.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.330
- You have a bad case of natural causes.

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:37.710
- First of all, he should do some tests,

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.450
but I wonder what they think it is.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:41.670
That's like one of the first
questions I ask as a doctor.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:45.390
- He's 102, his next test is an autopsy.

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:47.100
Look, I love the old man,

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.710
but I gotta get him out of the damn house.

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:53.340
He needs to be in a care facility.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:55.323
- So tell him, he's a big boy now.

00:01:57.778 --> 00:02:00.273
That's very generous, when you were 30.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.940
- [Patient's son]
Pretend to run the tests.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:06.930
- We don't do that.

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:08.190
You can't bribe doctors

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:09.720
to give you the results that you want.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.520
Doctors really shouldn't
be accepting gifts,

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:12.990
I think it's over $30,

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:14.250
I think that's what our tests say.

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:16.170
When a patient bakes
you a cake, it's fine,

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:17.400
but if a patient bakes you a cake

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.800
with gold flakes on
it, you have to say no.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:22.293
- I love him, but he can't let go.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:24.750
- 40 bucks says he can.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:28.050
- I can't do anything
without him helping me,

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.613
like I'm senile.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:33.960
- You're gonna give him five bucks.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:34.793
Oh no, he gave him 100.

00:02:34.793 --> 00:02:36.060
- Skip the blood work.

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:38.430
Tell my son it's grim news.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.830
I need to be in a nursing home.

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:42.990
- I think that's actually a dis.

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:45.360
If a patient thinks they can buy you,

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.550
that means you're sending
off the wrong signals,

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:50.670
and if two patients
think they can buy you,

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.620
that means you probably
should be retiring.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:54.739
- Test results.

00:02:54.739 --> 00:02:55.572
- Ha.

00:02:55.572 --> 00:02:57.510
- It's my recommendation
that you move into a home

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.920
with round the clock care.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:01.124
- I can't believe it.

00:03:01.124 --> 00:03:04.500
- Can't my son give me
round the clock care?

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:06.870
- Not unless you've done
your two year certification

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:09.090
in Tiburana swab technology.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:11.610
- Tiburana what technology?

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:12.450
That's made up.

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:14.670
- Just because he has a little tingling

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.010
and some trouble feeling hot and cold.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:19.830
- That's the spinal, oh my God,

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:22.140
the thalamic pathway of the spine.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.604
God, I don't remember
the pathways anymore.

00:03:23.604 --> 00:03:24.437
(computer pings)

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:25.500
- Show me your denture cream.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:28.590
He has zinc poisoning.

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:30.120
To get it from denture cream,

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.230
you'd have to take so much of it,

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.177
trust me, he never leaves home without it.

00:03:33.177 --> 00:03:34.740
- How much do you use, pop?

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.390
- About a tube a day.

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:37.950
- It explains all your symptoms.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:39.660
Medically, there's no
reason to go anywhere.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:40.620
- He solved the case

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.510
