00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:51.530
- You're not pregnant.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:54.578
- Well, I told you that.

00:04:54.578 --> 00:04:55.713
- You were pregnant.

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:59.130
Based on your hormone levels
you've had a miscarriage.

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:00.330
- Well, that could happen.

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:01.680
We can see that, yeah.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:03.390
- I haven't even been on a date.

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:06.060
- Right, since it's physically impossible

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:07.920
to have sex without
someone buying you dinner.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:09.240
- I haven't had sex.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:12.540
- Fine, have it your way,
immaculate conception.

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:15.630
- Or, how about this, Dr. House,

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:19.110
the patient has a tumor
that's secreting the hormone

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:22.410
that you think is responsible
for her lost pregnancy

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:25.320
and you think about her
cancer potential diagnosis

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:27.330
instead of assuming she's a liar.

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:28.923
- What do I do?

00:05:28.923 --> 00:05:32.580
- Well, it's obvious, start a religion.

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:34.200
- Take birth control if you truly believe

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.990
that she was pregnant as a
result of sexual activity.

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:38.190
- I've got your results back.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:40.194
No GHB, no nothing.

00:05:40.194 --> 00:05:43.050
It means you're having sex
and you're lying about it.

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:45.750
- No, I haven't had any in over a year.

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:48.210
I just wake up really exhausted.

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:49.740
- Oh my God is she sleepwalking?

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:52.650
- My ex lives in the apartment downstairs.

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:55.440
He's always calling me, always
wanting to get back together,

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.270
complaining about mixed signals.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:59.193
- We have a sleep lab in the basement.

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:01.920
If nothing else,

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:03.420
it'll get you away from
your ex for a night.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:05.250
- See, when I present
patients to a sleep lab

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:06.960
it's usually a diagnosis of sleep apnea,

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:09.510
which is, basically,
where you stop breathing

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:10.343
for a period of time

00:06:10.343 --> 00:06:11.400
and, as a result, you wake up

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.980
and you are not really able
to get good quality sleep.

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:15.750
And as a result you get increased risk

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:16.770
of all these other conditions

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:19.170
like hypertension, cardiac disease,

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:20.760
even diabetes in some cases.

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:23.640
- These were your brainwaves at 2:45 AM.

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:25.380
Here it comes, there's an abrupt jump

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:26.940
from slow wave sleep.

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:29.730
This indicates partial sleep arousal.

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:33.060
Most common type is
somnambulism, sleep walking.

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:35.730
- That would explain why
I'm so tired when I wake up.

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:38.790
- Yes, and also why you were pregnant.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:41.250
- I had sex in my sleep?

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:43.350
- Only in a medical drama.

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:46.920
- No formula, just mommy's
healthy, natural breast milk.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:49.260
- I hope you also
supplement with vitamin D,

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:51.930
400 IU or 10 micrograms.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:54.180
- Her whole face just got
swollen like this overnight.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:55.013
- Mm-hm?

00:06:56.070 --> 00:07:00.000
- Maybe a little slapped cheek,
a little parvo virus B19.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.735
- No fever, glands normal.

00:07:03.735 --> 00:07:07.140
- Do you go, glands normal?

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:09.443
My guy, feel the glands!

00:07:09.443 --> 00:07:10.620
(graphic beeps)

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:12.060
- Vaccination dates?

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:13.590
- We're not vaccinating.

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:16.290
- House, please handle
this with some empathy,

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:18.270
please, empathetic approach.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:19.230
- Think they don't work?

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:21.480
- I think some multinational
pharmaceutical company

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:24.210
wants me to think they
work, pad their bottom line.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:27.030
- You know another really good business?

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:29.429
Teeny, tiny baby coffins.

00:07:29.429 --> 00:07:32.929
(dramatic drumming music)

00:07:35.113 --> 00:07:35.946
(graphic buzzes)

00:07:35.946 --> 00:07:37.316
(speaking foreign language)

00:07:37.316 --> 00:07:39.060
- She has mental problems.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:40.170
They're really bad.

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:42.000
The pain keeps her in bed all day.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:44.520
Plus she's super depressed.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:47.520
- A red nose could be a
sign of a viral illness,

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:49.410
perhaps allergies, frequent rubbing.

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:51.630
Also, patient looks a little bit pale,

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:53.760
heavy menses with menstrual pain

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:56.130
could be related to fibroids.

00:07:56.130 --> 00:07:59.744
- She wants birth control
pills for her PMS.

00:07:59.744 --> 00:08:00.577
- I guess.

00:08:00.577 --> 00:08:01.410
- Or is she pregnant?

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:03.900
- Judging by the redness
around your mom's nostrils

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:05.070
and the tissue she's got

00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:06.750
conveniently stashed in her wristband,

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:08.883
I'd say her problem is more likely a URI.

00:08:09.729 --> 00:08:10.562
- A URI?

00:08:10.562 --> 00:08:11.730
- Upper respiratory infection.

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:13.650
- An Upper respiratory infection.

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:15.360
I also think she's got a problem with SAC

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:18.900
- SAC?
- Stupid American child.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:20.460
If you want the pill,

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:22.470
all you have to do is to
walk into any health clinic

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:24.287
in Jersey, alone, and ask for it.

00:08:24.287 --> 00:08:26.520
- How in the world did he know this?

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:29.880
I would rack my brain for days
trying to help the patient.

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:31.410
He just assumes the worst.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:34.133
How do you even function this way?

00:08:34.133 --> 00:08:35.075
(paper rips)

00:08:35.075 --> 00:08:36.630
- Is that for her cold?

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:38.730
- No, that's for your ovaries.

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:39.960
I assume you haven't had a stroke.

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:41.310
Have you ever had a blood clot?

00:08:41.310 --> 00:08:42.540
- No.
- Super.

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:46.357
- Also ask if she smokes
Dr. House, that's important.

00:08:46.357 --> 00:08:47.190
(speaking foreign language)

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:48.023
- She's been taking the decongestants

00:08:48.023 --> 00:08:49.140
but she's not getting better.

00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:50.724
She asks (speaks indistinctly)

00:08:50.724 --> 00:08:51.739
- What?

00:08:51.739 --> 00:08:54.210
- Her boobs are bigger.

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:55.560
- Is she taking the birth control?

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:57.510
- How could you get them mixed up?

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:59.010
They come in a little wheel.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:01.323
They don't look anything
like decongestants.

00:09:02.548 --> 00:09:05.340
(speaking foreign language)

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:07.743
No, you gave her the wrong pills.

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:10.560
- You speak Mandarin?

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:12.450
- What is happening in this episode?

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:13.650
He speaks every language.

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:14.790
He knows every body part.

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:18.303
He knows every snake poison and rat toe.

00:09:18.303 --> 00:09:20.081
- So, when did this start?

00:09:20.081 --> 00:09:22.290
- Couple of weeks ago.

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:23.760
I didn't wanna get pregnant.

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:26.373
Jake's not into rubbers,
so I got on the jelly.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:29.255
- You have an infection.

00:09:29.255 --> 00:09:30.088
I'm gonna need a sample.

00:09:30.088 --> 00:09:30.990
- I brought the jar.

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:33.090
- Wait, she is literally putting jelly?

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:36.210
- Okay, we have a
neurological problem here.

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:38.454
- There's something wrong with my brain?

00:09:38.454 --> 00:09:42.390
- Oh yeah, okay, I'm gonna
give you some antibiotics.

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:44.010
You probably shouldn't
have sex for a while.

00:09:44.010 --> 00:09:45.240
- How long?

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:48.330
- On an evolutionary basis,
I'd recommend forever.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:49.163
- So mean.

00:09:49.163 --> 00:09:50.400
I think it goes without saying,

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:53.790
